Here's how you can resolve this issue:

1. **Check XML Declaration**: Ensure that the `logback-spring.xml` file starts with a valid XML declaration. The first line should be:
   ```xml
   <?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
   ```

2. **Validate XML Structure**: Make sure the XML structure is correct and there are no misplaced characters or tags. The file should be well-formed XML.

3. **Check for Invalid Characters**: Sometimes, invisible characters or incorrect encoding can cause issues. Ensure the file is saved with UTF-8 encoding.

4. **Verify Logback Configuration**: Ensure that all Logback configuration elements are correctly specified. Here's a basic example of a Logback configuration:

   ```xml::logback-spring.xml::C:/Users/baira/OneDrive/Documents/AI_Projects/payment-system/payment-service/src/main/resources/logback-spring.xml
   <?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
   <configuration>
       <include resource="org/springframework/boot/logging/logback/defaults.xml"/>

       <!-- Console Appender with structured logging -->
       <appender name="CONSOLE" class="ch.qos.logback.core.ConsoleAppender">
           <encoder class="net.logstash.logback.encoder.LogstashEncoder">
               <providers>
                   <timestamp>
                       <timeZone>UTC</timeZone>
                   </timestamp>
                   <version/>
                   <logLevel/>
                   <hostname/>
                   <mdc/>
                   <thread/>
                   <logger/>
                   <loggerName/>
                   <levelValue/>
                   <callerData/>
                   <stackTrace/>
                   <message/>
                   <arguments/>
               </providers>
               <customFields>{"service":"payment-service","environment":"local"}</customFields>
           </encoder>
       </appender>

       <!-- File Appender with JSON format -->
       <appender name="FILE" class="ch.qos.logback.core.rolling.RollingFileAppender">
           <file>/logs/payment-service.log</file>
           <rollingPolicy class="ch.qos.logback.core.rolling.TimeBasedRollingPolicy">
               <fileNamePattern>/logs/payment-service-%d{yyyy-MM-dd}.log</fileNamePattern>
               <maxHistory>30</maxHistory>
               <totalSizeCap>1GB</totalSizeCap>
           </rollingPolicy>
           <encoder class="net.logstash.logback.encoder.LogstashEncoder">
               <providers>
                   <timestamp>
                       <timeZone>UTC</timeZone>
                   </timestamp>
                   <version/>
                   <logLevel/>
                   <hostname/>
                   <mdc/>
                   <thread/>
                   <logger/>
                   <loggerName/>
                   <levelValue/>
                   <callerData/>
                   <stackTrace/>
                   <message/>
                   <arguments/>
               </providers>
               <customFields>{"service":"payment-service","environment":"local"}</customFields>
           </encoder>
       </appender>

       <!-- Logger configurations -->
       <logger name="com.example.payment" level="DEBUG"/>
       <logger name="org.springframework.web" level="INFO"/>
       <logger name="org.springframework.amqp" level="INFO"/>
       <logger name="org.hibernate.SQL" level="DEBUG"/>
       <logger name="org.hibernate.type.descriptor.sql.BasicBinder" level="TRACE"/>

       <root level="INFO">
           <appender-ref ref="CONSOLE"/>
           <appender-ref ref="FILE"/>
       </root>
   </configuration>
   ```

5. **Rebuild the Project**: After making changes, rebuild your project to ensure the updated configuration is used.

If you continue to face issues, please ensure that the `logback-spring.xml` file is correctly placed in the `resources` directory of your project. If you have access to the file, reviewing its content for any anomalies would be beneficial.






